Create VPN

Once the device has picked up the certificates you can create the VPN connection

Open System Preferences and search for network

click into the network settings and then the three dots in the bottom right, from the options select IKEv2

The settings for the VPN connection;

Display Name - LBR VPN

Server Address - azuregateway-c3010072-1a9b-4cc7-82de-cca3ab6956ae-14c44a3d91d7.vpn.azure.com

Remote IT - azuregateway-c3010072-1a9b-4cc7-82de-cca3ab6956ae-14c44a3d91d7.vpn.azure.com

User Authentication - None

Machine Authentication - Certificate

you will need to check the certificate before selecting it in keychain access, double click the certificate and check the usage of it contains: "Usage Digital Signature, Key Encipherment"

Finish up by clicking Create, Test the VPN connection by connecting to TP-link or to mobile hotspot and connecting it.

Add the VPN to the menu bar on the MAC

System Settings > Control Centre > VPN > Show in Menu Bar

Amending the Hosts file

This is required to enable the user to access our fileshares

To amend the host file you will need to open it in terminal and edit it from there. To open it first open terminal and launch it as admin by running the following command then after run the command to open the host file

login

*sign in with localadmin*

sudo nano /etc/hosts

*enter localadmin password again*

